15. Qf3 Rac8 16. Bxf7+ Kh8 17. Qh3 Nxe5 18. Bxe5 Bxe5 19. Bxg6 e6 20. Rac1 cxb3
21. axb3 ({The bulletin clearly shows} 21. a3 {here but that would make no
sense, e.g. when White subsequently plays 32.Be8 when the residual b-pawn
would promote in two moves. This is a most unusual score error in an era when
scores are computer-generated and not typed in by hand as this one seems to
have been. One can only conclude that the original inputter who created the
bulletin made this error and failed to spot it when inputting the final few
moves of the game. It doesn't bode well for the accuracy of other scores from
this tournament!}) 21... Bxh2+ 22. Kh1 Be5 23. Be4 Qe7 24. Qh5 Qg7 25. Kg1 Bd6
26. Rxf8+ Rxf8 27. Rf1 a5 28. Rxf8+ Bxf8 29. Bd3 h6 30. Qg6 Qxg6 31. Bxg6 Kg7
