1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 c5 4. d5 d6 5. Nc3 exd5 6. cxd5 g6 7. Nd2 Bg7 8. Nc4
O-O 9. g3 b6 10. a4 Ne8 11. Bg2 Nd7 12. O-O Ba6 13. Na3 f5 14. Bd2 Ne5 15. Qc1
Nf6 16. Bh6 Qd7 17. Ra2 Bxh6 18. Qxh6 Nh5 19. Qc1 f4 20. Nab5 h6 21. b3 Rf7 22.
Ne4 Bxb5 23. axb5 Rd8 24. Qc3 Nf6 25. Nxf6+ Rxf6 26. Rfa1 Qxb5 27. gxf4 Rxf4
28. e3 Rb4 29. f4 Rxb3 30. Qc2 Nd3 31. Rxa7 c4 32. Rc7 Qe8 33. e4 Nxf4 34. Qxc4
Rc3 ({The bulletin continues} 34... Re3 35. Rg7+ ({If Black really had played .
..Re3, now} 35. Raa7 $1 {would have secured a draw.}) 35... Kh8 ({No reason
not to capture here, since after} 35... Kxg7 36. Qd4+ Qe5 $1 {and the a1 rook
is loose after the rook is captured}) 36. Qb4 Ne2+ 37. Kf2 Qf8+ 38. Kxe3 Qxg7 {
0-1, but it is wrong as pointed out by Harriet Hunt in a letter to BCM,
December 1996, p663. The actual moves given by her are given here.}) 35. Rg7+
Kh8 36. Qb4 Ne2+ 37. Kf2 Qf8+ 38. Kxe2 Qxg7 39. Rf1 {Source: bulletin as
corrected by Harriet Hunt letter to BCM, December 1996, p663} 0-1

